# Keep rules published to every consumer of :tdlib.
#
# TDLib's Java bindings are driven entirely from native code: `TdApi` request/response objects are
# instantiated field-by-field by `libtdjni.so`, and `Client`'s handlers are invoked from the TDLib
# thread. None of that is visible to R8, so the whole binding surface has to survive shrinking and
# renaming. `**` (not `*`) so the thousands of `TdApi$...` nested classes are covered explicitly.
-keep class org.drinkless.tdlib.** { *; }

# `Client`, `NativeClient` and `Secrets` declare `external`/`native` members that the .so resolves
# by their exact JNI signature.
-keepclasseswithmembernames,includedescriptorclasses class org.drinkless.tdlib.** {
    native <methods>;
}
